# Keep line endings LF on every platform. The emitters write '\n' and the CLI/goldens read and
# write in binary mode (no translation), so a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true would give
# CRLF golden files that no longer match LF-generated output -- every golden test would fail. Pin
# text to LF; mark the known binary fixtures so they are never touched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary test fixtures: wire payloads, the OSM PBF sample, images.
*.bin -text
*.pbf -text
*.png -text
*.ico -text
